  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "BREAKING\n- `GetCustomerInfo()` takes a `CustomerInfoFetchPolicy` before its `CancellationToken`: `GetCustomerInfo(CustomerInfoFetchPolicy fetchPolicy = CustomerInfoFetchPolicy.CachedOrFetched, CancellationToken cancellationToken = default)`. `GetCustomerInfo()` with no arguments compiles and behaves as before, but a call that passes only the token, `GetCustomerInfo(cancellationToken)`, no longer compiles - pass a policy first or name the argument (`GetCustomerInfo(cancellationToken: cancellationToken)`). Implementations of `IRevenueCatBilling` and mock setups such as `GetCustomerInfo(Arg.Any<CancellationToken>())` need the new parameter too.\n\nADDED\n- `CustomerInfoFetchPolicy` controls whether `GetCustomerInfo()` answers from the customer info the RevenueCat SDK caches on the device, which it treats as stale after 5 minutes in the foreground and after 25 hours in the background. Previously the wrapper always used the SDK default, which returns the cache even when stale, so a change made outside the app (a web purchase, a grant from the RevenueCat dashboard) could not be read on demand. https://github.com/Kebechet/Maui.RevenueCat.InAppBilling/issues/128\n  - `CachedOrFetched` (default) returns the cache even when stale and waits for a fetch only when nothing is cached. A stale cache is also refreshed in the background.\n  - `FetchCurrent` always fetches from RevenueCat.\n  - `NotStaleCachedOrFetched` returns the cache while it is fresh, otherwise fetches, and fails rather than returning stale data.\n  - `FromCacheOnly` never fetches, and fails with `CustomerInfoError` when nothing is cached.",
